{"id":"word:hebrew:H3091","type":"word","title":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","subtitle":"H3091 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Jehoshua (i.e. Joshua), the Jewish leader","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יְהוֹשׁוּעַ (H3091) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 218 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ (Yᵉhôwshûwaʻ) means Jehoshua (i.e. Joshua), the Jewish leader First listed occurrence: 1Chr 7 27."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","transliteration":"Yᵉhôwshûwaʻ","pronunciation":"yeh-ho-shoo'-ah","strong":"H3091","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3091","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ","יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ","יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ֙","יְהוֹשֻׁ֜עַ","יְהוֹשֻׁ֛עַ"],"morphs":[["HNp",196],["HC/Np",17],["HR/Np",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"Jehoshua (i.e. Joshua), the Jewish leader","usage":"Jehoshua, Jehoshuah, Joshua. Compare 1954 , 3442 .","full":"H3091. Yehoshua יְהוֺשֻׁעַ יְהוֺשׁוּעַ, and (later) יֵשׁוּעַ , proper name, masculine (& location, see 9 below) ( ׳י is salvation , or ׳י is opulence , compare אֲבִישׁוּעַ אֱלִישׁוּעַ, אֱלִישָׁע, & Nes SK 1892, 573 f. ; in any case it came to be associated with ישׁע , compare Matt 1:21 ; on יֵשׁוּעַ see especially Frä VOJ iv. 1890, 332 f. Müll SK 1892, 177 f. who cite analogue for change of ֹו to later ֵ֯ , & Nes l.c .) — 1 Moses' successor, son of Nun, ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) יְהוֺשׁוּעַ Deut 3:21 ; Judg 2:7 ; = יְהוֺשֻׁעַ Exod 17:9-10 , 13 , 14 ; 24:13 ; 32:17 ; 33:11 ; Num 11:28 ; 13:16 ; 14:6 , 30 , 38 ; 26:65 ; 27:18 , 22 ; 32:12 , 28 ; 34:17 ; Deut 1:38 ; 3:28 ; 31:3 , 7 , 14 (twice in verse); 31:23 ; 34:9 ; Josh 1:1 167t. Joshua; Judg 1:1 ; 2:6-7 , 8 , 21 , 23 ; 1Kin 16:34 ; 1Chr 7:27 ; = יֵשׁוּעַ Neh 8:17 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ); according to P, name changed by Moses from הוֺשֵׁעַ q. v. Num 13:8 , 16 ( ᵐ5 Αὑση ) Deut 32:44 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ). 2 יְהוֺשֻׁעַ a Bethshemite 1Sam 6:14 , 18 ( ᵐ5 'Wshe , A Ἰησοῦς , ᵐ5 L Ἰωσηε ). 3 high priest after the restoration, son of Jehozadak יְהוֺשֻׁעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) Hag 1:1 , 12 , 14 ; 2:2 , 4 ; Zech 3:1 , 3 , 6 , 8 , 9 ; 6:11 ; = יְשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ) Ezra 2:2 ; 3:2 , 8 ; 4:3 ; 5:2 ; 10:18 ; Neh 7:7 ; 12:1 , 7 , 10 , 26 . 4 יְהוֺשֻׁעַ governor of Jerusalem under Josiah 2Kin 23:8 ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς , ᵐ5 L Ἰωσηε ). 5 יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς ). head of one of the classes of priests 1Chr 24:11 , possibly also Ezra 2:36 = Neh 7:39 . 6 יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 Ἰησοῦς etc.), a Levitical family-name of frequent occurrence: a. Ezra 2:40 ; 3:9 = Neh 7:43 ; 8:7 ; 9:4-5 , 10:10 ; 12:8 . b. 2Chr 31:15 ; Ezra 8:33 ; Neh 12:24 . 7 יֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 id. ), father of a builder at the wall Neh 3:19 , perhaps = 8 a Judaite family-name ( ᵐ5 id. ), Ezra 2:6 = Neh 7:11 (compare Sm Listen 12 ). 9. proper name, of a location in south of Judah Neh 11:26 בְּיֵשׁוּעַ ( ᵐ5 ἐν Ἰησού , ᵐ5 L ἐν Σουα ). יֵשׁוּעַ יְהוֺשֻׁעַ, proper name .","rootNote":"or יְהוֹשֻׁעַ ; from 3068 and 3467 ; Jehovah-saved ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 7 27","keyReferences":["1Chr 7 27","1Kgs 16 34","1Sam 6 14","1Sam 6 18","2Kgs 23 8","Deut 1 38","Deut 3 21","Deut 3 28"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":218,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 7 27","book":"1Chr","chapter":7,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 34","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 18","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 8","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְהוֹשֻׁ֨עַ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"H